:: Felix Hang Out Park Playground Basic [nobr]

/* Intro */
<<set $Minutes += 20>>
As you and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span> walk over to the playground, his eyes catch a certain strange piece of equipment and he walks over. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh! What is this?”</span> He stops at something that is… difficult to describe. <span style="color:yellow">It is a bunch of large balls suspended by connecting metal rods that form almost a Christmas tree-like shape. You tilt your head at it curiously and say it reminds you of what people call ‘modern art’.</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span> raises an amused eyebrow at this and laughs. <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                    },
                },
                {
                Name: "Felix",
                State: {
                    Outfit: $HangOutClothes,
                    Mouth: "Smirk",
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“At a playground? No, I do not think so. I think it’s meant to be climbed! Look!”</span> He points to what do appear to be handles along the radius of the spheres, making it indeed seem to be climbable. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Come on! Let’s try to get to the top!”</span> As <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span> rushes over and begins to climb, you can’t get over how utterly strange this piece of equipment is. It may only go up about 6 feet, <span style="color:yellow">but it looks very strange and kind of like a falling hazard.</span> You wonder if it is some kind of statement or something someone made up, but it is indeed very real. Right here in front of you. <br>
<br>

<div id="choice">
	<<link "Watch Felix climb<br>">>
    <<replace"#choice">>
        You decide to stay on the ground rather than risk breaking your legs by climbing the absurdly designed climbing thing. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span> chuckles down at you as he reaches the halfway point. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Come on! It’s not that bad- woah!”</span> <span style="color:Pink"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span> loses his footing and nearly falls but manages to just hold on.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Okay, I had that coming!”</span> You laugh as he continues, determined to reach the top. <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:pink">The view isn’t that bad either, as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span> climbs and stretches at awkward angles, you get more than your fair share of interesting peeks and looks at everything from his stomach and sides to the waistband and even full peeks at his $FelixUndies.Name. It is a rather amusing sight.</span> <br>
        <br>
        As <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span> is nearing the top, you notice him stop curiously and glance around the ball. You call out what’s wrong and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span> shouts back <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“The top ball has no handle that I can see! How am I supposed to climb it?”</span> You reply that maybe he isn’t meant to get on top of the highest ball, <span style="color:yellow">but he doesn’t seem to accept that.</span> <br>
        
            <<set _ad to [
                {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Frown",
                    },
                },
                {
                Name: "Felix",
                State: {
                    Outfit: $HangOutClothes,
                    Mouth: "Smirk",
                    Eyes: "Mad",
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        Instead, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span> does his best to stand on the handles of the ball and leaps to the top one! <span style="color:yellow">You swear he is about to break his neck and cover your eyes in anticipation,</span> <span style="color:lightgreen">but he somehow, miraculously, manages to land on top of the sphere and hugs it tightly.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Haha! No one can be stopping me!”</span> <span style="color:lightgreen">You clap for <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span>, honestly impressed that he managed to reach the top without hurting himself.</span> <br>
        <br>
        Though as you hear him say <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Now, how am I to get down?”</span> you can’t help but break out laughing. <span style="color:lightgreen">He does eventually get down… after some effort.</span> <br>
        <<addMoodlet "Stress" 0>>
        <<needChange "Fun" 10>>
        <<socialChange "Felix" 3>>
        <span style="color:green">+Felix Fun</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Fun += 10>>
        <span style="color:red">-Felix Energy</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Energy -= 10>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Felix Hang Out Park]]
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
	<<link "Climb up the strange ball tree<br>">>
    <<replace"#choice">>
        You decide that safety and intact limbs are for cowards and follow behind <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span> to climb the absurdly designed tower. <span style="color:lightgreen">Afterall, kids are supposed to break their limbs trying new things… right?</span> <br>
        <br>
        It isn’t easy. The spheres aren’t exactly an easy shape to climb, even with the handles and flattened tops. <span style="color:yellow">You find yourself slipping more than once and only barely manage to keep hold and prevent yourself from falling.</span> <span style="color:lightgreen"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span> seems to be having an easier time, giving <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jackson</span> a run for his money as his climbing skills are pretty impressive.</span> He reaches just below the top before turning back and asking <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“How are you doing? We can go back down if you want.”</span> You know he is being genuinely kind, but you can’t help but take it as him thinking you’re not good enough. <span style="color:lightgreen">This spurs you to climb even harder and you soon reach the penultimate sphere just like him.</span> <br>
        
            <<set _ad to [
                {
                Name: "Player",
                State: {
                    Mouth: "Happy",
                    Blush: 1,
                    },
                },
                {
                Name: "Felix",
                State: {
                    Outfit: $HangOutClothes,
                    Mouth: "Smirk",
                    Eyes: "Mad",
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Haha, nice job! That wasn’t so hard, was it?”</span> He reaches out to give a fist bump, but you’re too nervous to let go of the sphere you are clinging to. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Alright, let us see.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span> looks up at the last sphere, though gives a curious expression upon realizing that it doesn’t have any sort of handle or grip point like the others. In fact, from what you can see the last sphere doesn’t look designed to be climbed on. Oh well, guess you guys got as far as you can. Time to- <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I got this!”</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:lightgreen"><span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Felix</span> says as he leaps from the sphere he is on directly on top of the highest ball like a mad man! You call out as he hits it hard but somehow manages to keep his grip.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Haha! I have conquered the tree of balls!”</span> He shouts out, <span style="color:Pink">giving you a smirk that shows he knows exactly what he’s saying.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Now… how do I get down?”</span> <br>
        <<addMoodlet "Stress" 0>>
        <<needChange "Fun" 15>>
        <<socialChange "Felix" 3>>
        <span style="color:green">+Felix Fun</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Fun += 10>>
        <span style="color:green">+Felix Comfort</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Comfort += 5>>
        <span style="color:red">-Felix Energy</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Energy -= 10>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|Felix Hang Out Park]]
    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
</div>